                <pb facs="0461" n="429" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v28/pg429"/>

                <head>213. Memorandum From James C.
                        Thomson of the National Security Council Staff to Vice President
                        Humphrey<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d213-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1965-12-21">December 21, 1965</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Helicopters for Laos</item>
                </list>
                <p>In response to your query of December 9th to Mac
                        Bundy<anchor n="2" xml:id="d213-f2"/> regarding Bill Sullivan’s
                    interest in meeting Souvanna’s request for more helicopters, here is a brief
                    status report:</p>
                <p>During his recent Saigon trip, Secretary McNamara decided to authorize delivery to the Laos Government of
                    a total of 10 helicopters (in addition to the 2 they already have) as rapidly as
                    the necessary ground and air crews can be found or trained. In fact, this will
                    mean delivery of two additional helicopters in January, with the remaining 8 to
                    be phased over an 18-month period. CINCPAC
                    has now proposed a specific timetable to implement McNamara’s decision.</p>
                <p>In short, Souvanna will be getting what he wants as rapidly as the Lao can
                    operate the helicopters—which is probably somewhat less rapidly than Souvanna
                    hopes.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#bold">James C. Thomson</hi>, Jr.<anchor n="3"
                            xml:id="d213-f3"/>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
